<p>The head of the International Atomic Energy Agency said in Seoul on Wednesday that North Korea is showing a “very serious increase” in its ability to produce nuclear weapons, pointing to signs of stepped-up activity at several nuclear facilities, including Yongbyon’s reactor, reprocessing unit and light-water reactor. Rafael Grossi also said the agency has seen what appears to be a new facility similar to the enrichment plant at Yongbyon, which could significantly expand uranium-enrichment capacity, though he stressed that without inspectors on the ground, the agency cannot calculate exact output. The warning matters because enriched uranium gives North Korea another path to weapons-grade material alongside plutonium reprocessing, and the country is already believed to have a few dozen warheads. North Korea has been under UN sanctions for its banned weapons programs since its first nuclear test in 2006, expelled IAEA inspectors in 2009, and says it will not give up its nuclear arsenal — a reminder of how difficult diplomacy and verification remain even as international monitors keep watch from outside the country.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/03TAmiomRtU84p_0keokrmqPZU7PlA6AEoSWakWk2zFbs4JUfuz0Ji66YA9dtsR18R4_On00A88LBJJPJmdeh8f-6CeIAswd2iq_FqPQAiV_' alt='North Korean leader Kim Jong Un visits the country’s nuclear material production base and nuclear weapons institute, at an undisclosed location in North Korea, in this photo released by North Korea’s official Korean Central News Agency on January 29, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Warhead estimate: Grossi said North Korea’s arsenal is estimated at a few dozen warheads, while The Guardian cited outside estimates of about 50, though some experts question whether Pyongyang can miniaturize them for long-range missiles.</li><li>Russia question: Asked whether Russia was helping North Korea’s nuclear development, Grossi said the IAEA had not seen “anything in particular” suggesting such assistance.</li><li>Yongbyon revival: South Korea’s spy agency says North Korea runs multiple uranium-enrichment facilities, including one at Yongbyon that Pyongyang had claimed to decommission before reactivating it in 2021.</li><li>Inspection gap: Grossi said outside monitoring can spot construction and operating patterns, but without access to the sites, the agency cannot precisely measure how much production has increased.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>IAEA: The agency says broader operations at Yongbyon and the appearance of a similar new enrichment facility show that North Korea is increasing its capacity to produce nuclear-weapons material, but it says on-site access is still necessary for an exact assessment. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3350206/un-watchdog-warns-north-korea-boosting-nuclear-weapons-capacity'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>North Korea: Pyongyang says it will never give up its nuclear weapons and has kept IAEA inspectors out since 2009, signaling that it sees its arsenal as non-negotiable. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/15/north-korea-showing-serious-increase-in-ability-to-make-nuclear-weapons-iaea-says'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Outside experts: Some experts cited by The Guardian doubt North Korea’s claims that it can miniaturize nuclear warheads for long-range ballistic missiles. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/north-korea-nuclear-weapons-capability-un-watchdog-rafael-grossi'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/east-asia/article/3350206/un-watchdog-warns-north-korea-boosting-nuclear-weapons-capacity'>UN watchdog warns North Korea is boosting nuclear weapons capacity</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/15/north-korea-showing-serious-increase-in-ability-to-make-nuclear-weapons-iaea-says'>North Korea showing &#x27;serious increase&#x27; in ability to make nuclear weapons, IAEA says</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/15/north-korea-nuclear-weapons-capability-un-watchdog-rafael-grossi'>North Korea rapidly expanding nuclear weapons capability, UN watchdog warns</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991947/north-korea-boosting-ability-to-make-nuclear-arms-un-watchdog'>North Korea boosting ability to make nuclear arms: UN watchdog</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/north-korea-is-boosting-nuclear-weapons-capacity-iaea-chief/article70864157.ece'>North Korea is boosting nuclear weapons capacity: IAEA chief</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.abs-cbn.com/news/world/2026/4/15/north-korea-showing-serious-increase-in-ability-to-make-nuclear-weapons-iaea-chief-1516'>International Atomic Energy Agency director general Rafael Grossi reports increased activity at multiple nuclear facilities in North Korea, including the Nyongbyon site, indicating expanded capacity to produce nuclear weapons.</a> - abs-cbn.com</li></ul>